Overall Attack / Problem-Solving Methodology

The Bandit challenges helped develop a repeatable approach:

Read the objective
       ↓
Inspect the environment
       ↓
Identify relevant files/data
       ↓
Determine the property of the data
       ↓
Select an appropriate Linux tool
       ↓
Process the result
       ↓
Verify the result
       ↓
Use the discovered information
       ↓
Move to the next level
Major Lessons
1. Enumeration before action

Before attempting random commands, inspect the environment and understand what is available.

2. Understand Linux tools

Commands such as find, grep, file, strings, sort, and uniq are powerful when their options are understood.

3. Combine commands

Linux pipes allow multiple tools to work together:

command1 | command2 | command3
4. Identify data before processing it

The file command can reveal what you're actually dealing with before choosing a tool.

5. Security requires problem solving

The challenges were not simply about memorizing commands.

The important skill was:

Determine what information is available, identify what is unusual, and choose the appropriate method to investigate it.

